VALUES (635, '1', $t$ASK 635: hydrogen's output-token limit is raised from 65,536 to 131,072$t$,
  $t$Give hydrogen enough output room that, after its reasoning, it can still write the judgment. In run 42517 hydrogen, as a panel judge, used 65,536 of 65,536 output tokens, 65,533 of them on reasoning, finished "length" and returned no text. Expected effect: when hydrogen judges, the reply ends "stop" with judgment text. Not promised: the record cannot show that 131,072 is enough; hydrogen has filled every limit it was given as a judge. No reasoning setting is touched. (plan rev 1, heading 1, ask635/w4/plan635.md md5 a9fa07cf)$t$,
  'not yet',
  $t$Written by W4 at 05:14 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's press "Write it" on W4's card (written, Wall 11971; audit 42082), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11975). One value in one row: model_config seat hydrogen (google/gemini-4-hydrogen) max_tokens 65,536 to 131,072, guarded on the prior value; a note line holds the undo value 65536. No engine or child node, no reasoning, temperature or model id, and no other seat changed. NOT YET, because the objective is hydrogen returning a verdict as a judge and no run has been made since the write. W4's search (plan heading 3): Resolve Seats and Panel Build pass max_tokens to the request with floors and no cap; the judge call's timeout is 900 s and the engine stops waiting at 980 s. W4's measure from one call: 65,536 tokens took about 343 s in run 42517, so a full 131,072 would take about 690 s, a guess against a 900 s timeout; a full judge call at the new limit costs about 1.10 dollars. The three legitimate results on a run where hydrogen judges (plan C3): (a) the reply ends "stop" with a stored judgment; (b) the ASK 629 line "returned no text: finish_reason length; output tokens 131,072", which means 131,072 is not enough; (c) a time-out, which means the limit is too high for the time allowed. (b) and (c) go back to the operator. W1's notes on the plan (Wall 11960): N1 Panel Judges Parallel has a 60 s timeout (it only dispatches); N2 the criteria should name the time-out outcome; N3 the operator's quotation was not checked by W1. Plan criterion C2 (an offline replay of Resolve Seats and Panel Build with the new row) was to run before the card and was SKIPPED, W4's stated mistake (Wall 11980); W4 ran it after the write, at 05:25 CST 2026-11-25: 5 PASS, 0 FAIL, the live Resolve Seats on the 42517 inputs gives the hydrogen judge 131,072 and nothing else in its output changes; Panel Build was checked from its code, not replayed. W1 reproduced it, 5 PASS with identical output (Wall 11982). NOT SEARCHED by W4: OpenRouter's per